# NOTE: an earlier version of this file listed itself, plus README.md,
# SETUP.md, PLAN.md and .env.example, which meant none of them were ever
# committed. A fresh clone therefore had no .gitignore at all and nothing
# stopping the next person from committing keys/sa.json. Do not re-add
# entries for tracked project files here.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# secrets: never commit credentials
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
keys/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# service account keys and similar, wherever they end up
*sa.json
*service-account*.json
*credentials*.json
*client_secret*.json
gha-creds-*.json
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# dbt build artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
target/
dbt_packages/
logs/
.user.yml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# local data and warehouses (ADR 0001: the Parquet raw zone is local and
# is never committed, regardless of how small it looks)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal
*.db
*.sqlite
*.parquet

# The published export (ADR-8). Regenerated wholesale by `make publish` from
# the warehouse, so it is a build artifact rather than a source, and it is
# large: mart_activity_by_h3 alone is a quarter of a million rows. The whole
# point of publishing is that it goes to a bucket, not into git.
published/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# os and editor noise
#
# .DS_Store has been here from the start and is why none has ever been
# committed. It is NOT why two of them are in the bucket: `gcloud storage`
# does not read this file, and the hand sync of the raw zone on 2026-08-01
# carried data/raw/.DS_Store and data/raw/raw_311_cases/.DS_Store up with the
# Parquet. Deleting them there is a bucket command, not a git one. Since PLAN-4
# step 6 the writer uploads objects itself and nothing syncs a directory, so
# the route that made them is closed; the two that exist are residue.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
USER-NOTES.md
